Description: Fix generated DH-parameter include for OpenSSL 1.0.x builds
 This patch is applied only when building with a dedicated EOL packaging
 overlay (debian.jessie/, debian.stretch/); build.sh skips all legacy_*
 patches for the modern distributions.
 .
 '#include "dh.h"' resolves to the system <openssl/dh.h> via
 -I/usr/include/openssl before it can reach the generated
 ../include/dh.h. On OpenSSL >= 1.1.0 this is harmless because
 AUTO_SSL_DH (SSL_CTX_set_dh_auto) skips the include entirely; on
 OpenSSL 1.0.x (jessie) the static-dh path is compiled and the wrong
 header leaves get_dh2048() undeclared, breaking the link. Use a path
 relative to the source file instead.
 .
 Note: the TLS floor is NOT relaxed for the EOL builds - OpenSSL 1.0.1
 (jessie) and 1.1.0 (stretch) both implement TLS 1.2, so the shipped
 default stays ssl_version=TLSv1.2+. Administrators supporting
 pre-TLS-1.2 clients can set 'ssl_version=TLSv1+' in nrpe.cfg.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/src/nrpe.c
+++ b/src/nrpe.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@

 #ifdef HAVE_SSL
 # if defined(USE_SSL_DH) && !defined(AUTO_SSL_DH)
-#  include "dh.h"
+#  include "../include/dh.h"
 # endif
 #endif
